          {
            "text": "Eliminating opponents in *Call of Duty* depends on mastering the core gameplay mechanics. Here are the primary ways to secure kills, along with tips to do it consistently:\n\n### 1. Weapon Combat (Guns)\n* **Hit the High-Damage Zones:** Aim for the upper chest and head. Headshots deal significantly more damage and decrease your Time-to-Kill (TTK).\n* **Aim Down Sights (ADS):** Hip-firing (shooting without aiming) is only effective at point-blank range. Always ADS when engaging targets at medium to long distances for better accuracy.\n* **Control Recoil:** Every gun has a recoil pattern (usually kicking upward). Pull down slightly on your right analog stick (controller) or mouse while firing to keep your shots on target.\n\n### 2. Melee Attacks\n* **Gun Bash / Knife:** If you are within arm's reach of an enemy, pressing the melee button (usually **R3/RS** on controllers or **E/F/V** on PC, depending on your keybinds) will strike the enemy. \n* **Finishing Moves:** Sneak up directly behind an unaware enemy and **press and hold** the melee button to trigger an instant-kill execution animation.\n\n### 3. Lethal Equipment\n* **Frag Grenades / Semtex:** Good for clearing out rooms or throwing at objectives. Cook frag grenades (hold the throw button briefly) so enemies have less time to escape the blast.\n* **Proximity Mines / Claymores:** Place these around high-traffic corners or behind you to defend a position.\n* **Throwing Knives:** Provide an instant elimination if you land a direct hit.\n\n### 4. Killstreaks / Scorestreaks\n* As you get kills or play the objective without dying, you unlock streaks (e.g., UAV, Cruise Missile, VTOL, Chopper Gunner). Deploying these can wipe out multiple enemies quickly.\n\n---\n\n### Key Tips to Win More Gunfights:\n* **Centering:** Keep your crosshairs pointed at head/chest level around corners where enemies are likely to appear, rather than looking at the ground while sprinting.\n* **Check the Minimap:** Watch for red dots (enemies firing unsuppressed weapons) and listen for footsteps to anticipate enemy positions before they see you.\n* **Use Cover:** Never challenge an enemy out in the open if you can avoid it. Fire from behind barriers so only your head and upper chest are exposed.",
